{
  "title": "Request path",
  "description": "HTTP clients enter the Fiber boundary with request correlation, logging, security headers and CORS. Public routes branch before token authentication and the per-IP limiter, which uses local memory or optional shared Redis. Protected plan routes reach the reasoning service; only the JSON route supports Idempotency-Key replay, while the stream route returns SSE. Topic, prerequisite path and cognitive graph routes read the in-memory graph. MCP over stdio enters the same service directly without HTTP middleware. The service validates and fans out work, reads the graph, and applies concurrency and circuit breaking before the BAML provider registry calls Amazon Bedrock by default, OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Ollama or an OpenAI-compatible server. HTTP, MCP and reasoning spans can be exported through optional OTLP and LangSmith exporters.",
